# Task 3: Many-to-Many Relationship using JPA

## Definition

Many-to-Many means:

* One student can have many courses
* One course can have many students

## Implementation

A join table is created to connect both entities.

## Student Entity

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import java.util.List;

@Entity
public class Student {

```
@Id
@GeneratedValue
private Long id;

private String name;

@ManyToMany
@JoinTable(
    name = "student_course",
    joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "student_id"),
    inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "course_id")
)
private List<Course> courses;
```

}

## Course Entity

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import java.util.List;

@Entity
public class Course {

```
@Id
@GeneratedValue
private Long id;

private String title;

@ManyToMany(mappedBy = "courses")
private List<Student> students;
```

}

## Join Table Structure

## student_course

student_id | course_id

## How It Works

student.getCourses().add(course);

This automatically creates a record in the join table.
